It does not provide any information about free HTTPS hosting with PHP support. If you’re looking for hosting, the closest supported guidance is that PHP and cURL/HTTPS were being used on a server, but no host recommendations are given here.

If you just need a short domain to point to a longer URL, the options covered here are frame forwarding, an HTTP redirect, or DNS-level forwarding. For a PHP-based redirect, the example shown is:

<?php
header("location: http://www.sitwithlongurl.com/evenlongerbit");
die;
?>

That means you’d need hosting that supports PHP. The evidence doesn’t list specific free HTTPS hosts with PHP support, so I can’t name one from this alone. The closest guidance is: look for free hosting that explicitly includes PHP, then use an HTTP redirect page on it.
